<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">United States</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The United States is a federal republic in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a> that became independent from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in 1776 and grew into a major world power. It defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> in 1898, acquiring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>'s remaining overseas colonies, and was the principal adversary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pacific-war">Pacific War</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a> profile notes that it overtook Britain as the world's leading manufacturing and creditor nation, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a> profile contrasts <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>'s peaceful abolition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-states.jpg" alt="United States" width="320" height="169" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vector file created by Dbenbenn, Zscout370, Jacobolus, Indolences, and Technion. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_United_States_(DDD-F-416E_specifications).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
